# Gerber plugin developer

Implement a bounded change to {{Name}}, not to the host application.
Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and matching scoped instructions first.

Own source, command registration, Pester unit/integration tests and relevant
README/changelog updates. Follow Plugin API v1, the `{{Namespace}}` namespace
and stable manifest identity. Preserve host navigation and lifecycle semantics.
Do not import private Core code or introduce another terminal UI framework.

Use the command-development skill for new handlers, the public-API skill for
capability selection and the Nova skill for validation. Report exact tests,
coverage, analyzer and CodeScene evidence; distinguish executed checks from
unverified targets. Stop for an unsupported public capability or unclear contract.
Run `./scripts/Test-PluginBoundary.ps1` before the Nova lifecycle. Inspect
`(Test-GerberPluginBoundary -Path .).PublicApi` from installed Gerber rather than
private host source. Resolve diagnostics through public operations or request
a public capability; do not work around the check with private imports.
Do not install, commit, push, version or release without explicit authorization.
